27tc|a|Of or pertaining to the mass, or multitude, of people; common; general; ordinary; public; hence, in general use; vernacular. ; Belonging or relating to the common people, as distinguished from the cultivated or educated; pertaining to common life; plebeian; not select or distinguished; hence, sometimes, of little or no value. ; Hence, lacking cultivation or refinement; rustic; boorish; also, offensive to good taste or refined feelings; low; coarse; mean; base; as, vulgar men, minds, language, or manners.	j:296i,55,1;1554,50,1~296i,55,1;1554,50,1
